jobs.description:
To further grow our Modern Data Platform Practice, we are currently looking for a skilled Power BI Expert.

Do you have at least 3 years of experience in designing and building data solutions with Power BI? You want to further develop your abilities & knowledge by working together with highly skilled, helpful and fun colleagues? You are not afraid to be challenged intellectually and personally?

If so, send us your CV and we’ll contact you for an interview and a cup of coffee.


Your responsibilities

• You’re able to work independently on a Power BI assignment;
• Analyze user requirements and design business intelligence solutions;
• Model the data according to business and technical requirements;
• Perform data analysis and generate insights;
• Create visualizations and dashboards;
• Actively participate in knowledge building and sharing;
• Stay up to date with new features and releases in Power BI (and Fabric);
• 
Communicate findings and insights effectively to stakeholders.



Your qualifications

• A minimum of 3 years of experience in speaking with and understanding the needs of clients;
• Between 3 and 5 years of experience with visualization tools such as Power BI and/or Tableau and/or Qlik and/or Looker;
• Experience with DAX, Power Query and SQL
• Hands-on experience with data modeling;
• Knowledge of best practices in Power BI for both data visualization and VertiPaq internals;
• Familiarity with ETL processes and data warehousing concepts;
• Fluent in Dutch and/or French and English;
• Strong communication and interpersonal skills;
• Problem-solving abilities and attention to detail.

Your growth path

• Further grow our Modern Data Platform Practice;
• Continuous learning on projects as well as through training;
• Participate in knowledge building through our competence centers;
• Gradually, you’ll assume more responsibility and grow to a coaching role for more junior colleagues

At Datashift, we believe in the power of data science, analytics and artificial intelligence to solve the complex challenges in today's industries. We advise our clients based on actionable insights that drive decision-making and sustainable business value creation. As a data strategy consultant, you will play a crucial role in developing strategies for business growth through analytics for our clients.


Your responsibilities
As a Data & AI Strategy Consultant, you will:

• Collaborate with client stakeholders to identify and clarify key business challenges that could benefit from data & analytics;
• Be the crucial link between AI/data science teams and business units to translate these insights into clear business terms and strategies, and to ensure that the proposed solutions are actionable and relevant;
• Oversee analytics projects from ideation to execution to guarantee they serve the overall business goals;
• Proactively inspire and advise client & internal stakeholders on data & AI-related initiatives;
• 
Stay informed about industry trends and advancements in data science and AI.



Your qualifications
• Master’s degree (Business engineering, Computer Science, Information Systems, Business Analytics,...);
• A first experience in a strategy role in a consulting firm or a highly dynamic business environment is considered a must;
• Understanding of and interest in the impact of data and AI in industries and organizations;
• A strategic thinker with a strong analytical mindset;
• Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively with stakeholders at all levels in an organization;
• 
A fluent level of English is a must. Dutch is considered a big plus.
